<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">André Masséna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1758">1758</a>–<a href="/years/1817">1817</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Andre Massena</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">André Masséna was a French general of the Revolutionary and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a>, made a Marshal of the Empire in 1804. He won the Second Battle of Zurich in 1799, held besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> for two months in 1800, and fought at Aspern-Essling and Wagram in 1809. His invasion of Portugal was halted at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lines-of-torres-vedras">Lines of Torres Vedras</a> in 1810–11.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andre-massena.jpg" alt="André Masséna" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edme-Adolphe Fontaine / After Antoine-Jean Gros · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andr%C3%A9_Mass%C3%A9na_(Fontaine_et_Gros).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
